From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rory Axton <roryaxton@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:06:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] 0911 redfin: GIC SPIs for SWEET drivers; sec_ts touch on its interrupt

sweet_spi_attach/mask/dispatch from sailfish 0181 (after HackiOS's
gic_v3_spi_attach): a SWEET driver configures, routes and enables a GIC
SPI, and sleh_irq hands it the INTID. sec_ts takes the TLMM summary
interrupt (SPI 208 = INTID 240) for its attention pin gpio9 instead of
waking every 8 ms. It falls back to polling if the line is seen low with
no interrupt, or if another pin storms the summary. sectouchirq=0 polls.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GizUhEzkc6MoTcLnCZCfFa
---
  osfmk/arm64/sleh.c   |  8 ++++-
  pexpert/arm/pe_fiq.c | 76 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
  bsd/dev/sweet_sects.c | 92 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----

